Subject: clear the new HTree leaf block and checksum it last

ext4_dir_dx_init() creates the first leaf block of a newly indexed directory.
Two problems, both visible as "directory passes checks but fails checksum" from
e2fsck:

1. The block is obtained with ext4_trans_block_get_noread(), which returns the
   cache slot as-is, and the comment "Fill the whole block with empty entry"
   was never actually implemented -- there is no memset. Everything past the
   first entry header keeps whatever the buffer previously held, so stale bytes
   are written to disk inside a directory block.

2. ext4_dir_set_csum() ran *before* the final ext4_dir_en_set_inode(be, 0).
   That last store mutates a field the checksum covers, so the stored checksum
   describes a block that no longer exists.

The two interact, which is why this hides in ordinary builds: when the cache
slot happens to be zeroed, set_inode(be, 0) writes a value that is already
there, the block does not change, and the stale checksum still matches. Build
with -O0 -fsanitize=address, where the slot holds non-zero data, and every
mkdir on a dir_index volume produces a directory whose checksum is wrong.

Clearing the block and moving the checksum to the end fixes both.

Reproducer, on any ext4 volume with dir_index + metadata_csum (the mke2fs
default):

    mkdir /a
    e2fsck -fn image
    -> Directory inode 524, block #1: directory passes checks but fails checksum.

diff --git a/src/ext4_dir_idx.c b/src/ext4_dir_idx.c
index f916cc6..e1ab08f 100644
--- a/src/ext4_dir_idx.c
+++ b/src/ext4_dir_idx.c
@@ -433,19 +433,28 @@ int ext4_dir_dx_init(struct ext4_inode_ref *dir, struct ext4_inode_ref *parent)
 	/* Fill the whole block with empty entry */
 	struct ext4_dir_en *be = (void *)new_block.data;
 
+	/*
+	 * block_get_noread() hands back whatever was in the cache slot, so the
+	 * block must be cleared before use. Otherwise the bytes past the first
+	 * entry keep stale contents, which both leaks them to disk and makes
+	 * the directory checksum depend on uninitialised memory.
+	 */
+	memset(be, 0, block_size);
+
+	ext4_dir_en_set_inode(be, 0);
+
 	if (ext4_sb_feature_ro_com(sb, EXT4_FRO_COM_METADATA_CSUM)) {
 		uint16_t len = block_size - sizeof(struct ext4_dir_entry_tail);
 		ext4_dir_en_set_entry_len(be, len);
 		ext4_dir_en_set_name_len(sb, be, 0);
 		ext4_dir_en_set_inode_type(sb, be, EXT4_DE_UNKNOWN);
 		ext4_dir_init_entry_tail(EXT4_DIRENT_TAIL(be, block_size));
+		/* Checksum last: it must cover the finished block. */
 		ext4_dir_set_csum(dir, be);
 	} else {
 		ext4_dir_en_set_entry_len(be, block_size);
 	}
 
-	ext4_dir_en_set_inode(be, 0);
-
 	ext4_trans_set_block_dirty(new_block.buf);
 	rc = ext4_block_set(dir->fs->bdev, &new_block);
 	if (rc != EOK) {
